{
 "note": "Three repeats of the 1.0.0 --workers sweep (2 and 4 workers, clean_mlp and bert_small, c=8 and c=32, result cache off). 12 server starts: 3 never became ready; 18 windows: 3 had a request that timed out. CAUSE: the harness started each server with stdout=PIPE and never read it. A Windows pipe holds about 4 KB; when it was full, the next log write blocked (py-spy: the 'downshift-loader' thread sat in print_ready -> logger.info -> write; under load a log write blocked a request). The harness now writes server output to a temp file (bench/run.py spawn_server). 'after_fix' is one sweep with the fix: 4 server starts, 8 windows, 0 errors; a loop of 12 starts of clean_mlp --workers 2 had 0 hangs. downshift is not at fault.",
